# Go Quality Bar

- Keep conversion logic in `internal/convert` and CLI wiring in `internal/cli`; `cmd/giffer` stays a thin main.
- Prefer table-driven tests; cover SPEC edge cases (bad zip, no images, invalid flags, sort order, resize).
- Do not commit files under `upload/` (except `upload/.gitkeep`); use tiny synthetic fixtures in tests.
- Before finishing Go changes, run `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...`. Prefer `make check` when Make is available.
- Cross-platform release binaries go under `release/<platform>/` via `make release` (for example `release/windows-amd64/giffer.exe`); do not commit loose `.exe` files outside `release/`. Bump semver in docs and tag before shipping (see `semver-bump.mdc`).
- Use `cli.Run` for command tests; do not shell out to the binary in unit tests.
